  "caption": "Proof outline for 3-Majority in the case where $\\alphanorm_0\\geq C(\\log n)/\\sqrt{n}$. \n    Here, $C>0$ denotes a sufficiently large constant, $c\\in (0,1)$ denotes a sufficiently small constant, and $c_*>0$ denotes an arbitrary constant.\n    Throughout this proof outline, we use \\cref{lem:taunormdown is large} to ensure $\\alphanorm_t\\geq C(1-\\cnormdown)(\\log n)/\\sqrt{n}$ in a sufficiently long period. \n    The proof for 2-Choices follows a similar outline."
